.env

# Compiled binaries (local and CI outputs)
bin/
/north-web
/north-worker
/north-mcp
/main
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# `go build ./cmd/worker/` writes its output here, named after the package
# directory rather than the names above. A 50 MB binary reached main this way
# once; `git add -A` does not know the difference.
#
# Not `/web`: that is the templates directory. `go build ./cmd/web/` cannot
# write there anyway, because the directory already exists.
/worker
/mcp-server

# `go build ./cmd/...`-adjacent strays. `templ` is the templ CLI the browser
# app used to generate with; a manual `go build` of it wrote 20 MB of Mach-O
# here once.
/templ

# tools/model is a build-time Node tool, run by hand and never deployed
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Go module vendoring, at the repository root only. Unanchored, this pattern
# also matched web/assets/js/vendor — the committed third-party JavaScript —
# so every file in there had to be force-added, and one that was not would go
# missing with no error until a page tried to load it.
/vendor/
# Local scratch output.
tmp/
